# Decisions Log

## DEC-2026-06-13-001

Decision: Adopt baseline v1 retrofit artifacts on branch `retrofit/baseline-v1` from backup tag `pre-retrofit-20260613T075234Z`.

Rationale: The retrofit bundle requires a reversible baseline before further production-readiness changes.

## DEC-2026-06-13-002

Decision: Normalize copied bundle text for source-text gates while preserving original archive hashes in `spec/BUNDLE_SOURCE_MANIFEST.md`.

Rationale: The repository rejects BOMs, em dashes, and replacement characters in tracked source text.

## DEC-2026-06-13-003

Decision: Keep T1 additive and docs-only; defer existing source/config changes to later tiers.

Rationale: The safest production-readiness step is to create stable shared context and rollback points before editing executable surfaces.

## DEC-2026-06-13-004

Decision: Pin the CI global Melos activation to 7.8.1, matching the root workspace dependency and lockfile.

Rationale: CI must execute the same orchestration version as the local workspace; the previous 7.5.1 pin could produce divergent command behavior.

## DEC-2026-08-09-005

Decision: Upgrade the workspace and CI Melos baseline to 8.2.2 and refresh compatible transitive lockfile versions.

Rationale: The current Flutter/Dart toolchain resolved Melos 8.2.2 and `mustache_template` 2.0.5, clearing all actionable dependency audit items while preserving the existing package constraints.

## DEC-2026-08-09-006

Decision: Add the mobile Android host behind the existing generic secure-key
method-channel contract, using Android Keystore AES-GCM encryption and durable
namespace-bound preference records. Release signing must be supplied through
operator-owned environment values and never defaults to debug keys.

Rationale: The repository already locked the app/native boundary and receipt
key-ring seams. A platform implementation can now satisfy that contract
without moving receipt policy into `peerdeal_native_bridges` or committing
credentials to source.

## DEC-2026-08-09-007

Decision: Add the Windows desktop host behind the existing generic secure-key
method-channel contract, using Windows Credential Manager with a namespace-
derived target and a bounded versioned record envelope. Keep receipt purposes,
algorithms, and rotation policy in app/receipt code.

Rationale: Windows is the available desktop target and provides an OS-managed
per-user credential boundary without adding a package or persisting key
material in app files. The host can satisfy the existing app key-ring seam
while keeping runtime profile validation and other platform work explicit.
